ing mistaken for a pipeline that repeatedly discovers unrelated winners."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"deep-dive","className":"article-prose deep-dive","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Choose the denominator before celebrating"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A hit rate is a fraction with politics hidden inside it. Suppose a team counts only published posts while quietly excluding abandoned edits, failed uploads and accounts it retired. That might be a reasonable publishing metric, but it is not the success rate of the entire operation. Define what qualifies as an attempt and what qualifies as a hit before the reporting period starts. Keep those definitions stable. If you move the threshold downward after a weak month, the chart becomes an argument for keeping the project alive rather than a useful description."}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"editorial-diagram diagram-compare","children":[["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"THE IDEA, UNPACKED"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Three decisions inside one fraction"}]]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"diagram-items","children":[["$","li","Attempt",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Attempt"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Which published, failed or abandoned units count?"}],false]}]]}],["$","li","Threshold",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"02"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Threshold"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"What outcome qualifies, and at what age?"}],false]}]]}],["$","li","Scope",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"03"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Scope"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Does the rate describe posts, accounts or campaigns?"}],false]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"diagram-caption","children":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."}]]}],[["$","p","0",{"children":"Report the number of attempts alongside the fraction. Two hits in a tiny batch and twenty in a much larger batch carry different uncertainty, even when the displayed percentage matches. Separate account-level concentration from post-level frequency: one unusually successful account can make a network look broadly healthy. Keep a second measure for meaningful downstream behaviour so entertainment reach does not silently become purchase intent. The point of this metric is to compare a defined process over time, not to turn a rare event into a promise."}]]]}],false,false,"$L19","$undefined","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d"]}],"$L1e"]}]
